# Mule Flow & Subflow Naming Standards

When reviewing Mule XML flow files, enforce these naming rules:

## Flow File Names
- Must be **all lower-case**, separated by **hyphens** (dashes)
- No underscores, no camelCase, no spaces
- Example: `address-validation.xml`, `global-error-handler.xml`

## Flow Names
- Format: `{descriptive-name}-flow` — all lower-case, hyphen-separated, suffixed with `-flow`
- Examples: `aspn-events-flow`, `common-connectivity-usps-request-flow`
- The **main** flow must be `{api-spec-name}-main` (e.g., `na-sfl-exp-api-spec-main`)

## Sub-Flow Names
- Format: `{descriptive-name}-sub-flow` — all lower-case, hyphen-separated, suffixed with `-sub-flow`
- The name should relate to the file name or the operation it performs
- Examples: `address-validation-sub-flow` (in `address-validation.xml`), `alive-sub-flow` (in `alive.xml`), `check-for-raise-error-sub-flow`

## Message Processor Display Names (`doc:name`)
- **Never** leave default Anypoint Studio names on processors (e.g., "Transform Message", "Set Variable"). Exception: Try/Catch scopes and error handlers may keep defaults
- Use descriptive, readable names in Title Case or natural language:
  - **Transform**: use a descriptive name (e.g., `Set Target API Params`, `Set Aliveness Response`). *Optional (minor):* prefix with `FV` for variable-setting transforms or `DW` for payload transforms
  - **Flow Reference**: use the referenced flow/sub-flow name (e.g., `alive-sub-flow`, `patient-mq-publish-sub-flow`)
  - **HTTP Request**: describe the target system (e.g., `REQUEST USPS SYS API`)
  - **Custom Logger** (`module-logger`): describe the log point (e.g., `Log Entry`, `Log Exit`, `Log Before Request`, `Log Error`, `Log Platform Event Received`)
  - **Set Variable**: describe what is being set (e.g., `Set HTTP Status Code`)
  - **Scopes** (Try/Catch): default names (e.g., `Try`, `On Error Continue`, `On Error Propagate`) are acceptable. *Optional (minor):* use descriptive names (e.g., `Try DLQ Publish`, `DLQ Publish Failed`)
  - **Choice**: describe the condition (e.g., `CHECK for Success == false`)

## APIKit-Generated Flows
- **Do not rename** flows generated by APIKit scaffolding — the router depends on these exact names
- These follow the pattern `{method}:\{resource}:{api-config}` (e.g., `get:\ping:na-sfl-exp-api-spec-config`)
- Replace hardcoded example response transforms with flow references to implementation sub-flows

## Review Checklist
- [ ] Flow file name is lower-case-hyphenated
- [ ] Flows suffixed with `-flow`, sub-flows with `-sub-flow`
- [ ] Main flow named `{api-spec-name}-main`
- [ ] No processors left with default Studio names
- [ ] Processor display names are descriptive (prefix conventions `FV`/`DW` are optional — minor)
